According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Kid Footwear market was valued at USD 40,060 million in 2024 and is projected to reach USD 59,490 million by 2034, growing at a CAGR of 6.0% during the forecast period (2024-2034). This steady growth reflects rising disposable incomes, increasing awareness about children's foot health, and evolving fashion trends in youth footwear categories.
What is Kid Footwear?
Kid footwear refers to shoes specifically engineered for children aged 0-12, combining developmental support with style elements that appeal to both parents and young wearers. These products incorporate specialized features like flexible soles for natural foot movement and adjustable closures to accommodate growing feet. The market offers diverse categories including:
•	Everyday casual shoes for school and play
•	Athletic footwear optimized for sports and physical activities
•	Seasonal footwear including sandals and winter boots
•	Special occasion shoes for formal events
